.TH "GH-PR.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gh\-pr.sh \- interactive GitHub pull request creation helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBgh\-pr.sh\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prompt for a branch name, commit message, PR title and PR body; open the configured editor for the body; then, after confirmation, create a branch, stage all files with git add ., commit, push and open a PR using gh. It can optionally switch back to the original branch and merge or rebase locally.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBEDITOR\fR
Editor used to prepare the PR description (defaults to vim).
.SH NOTES
IMPORTANT: This helper stages all files, not only selected changes. Confirm the working tree is appropriate before using it.
.PP
The optional merge/rebase is a local Git operation, not a GitHub PR merge. Use this helper only when that workflow is intended.
.SH SEE ALSO
gh(1), git(1)
